CHAPTER VIII
SPECIAL PROTECTION OF CHILDREN
Article 15
(1) Special protection of children is provided to:
a. children in emergency situations;
b. children in conflict with the law;
c. children from minority and isolated groups;
d. children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic substances, and other addictive substances abuse;
f. children who are victims of pornography;
g. children with HIV/AIDS;
h. children victims of abduction, sale, and/or trafficking;
i. children victims of physical and/or psychological violence;
j. children victims of sexual crimes;
k. children victims of terrorist networks;
l. children with disabilities;
m. children victims of maltreatment and neglect;
n. children with deviant social behavior; and
o. children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition.
(2) The Regional Government in implementing the handling of special protection of children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 4
The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence and discrimination are:
a. to prevent acts of violence and discrimination against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. to eliminate all forms of violence, discrimination, and exploitation against women and children;
c. to protect women and children from acts of violence and discrimination in obtaining their constitutional rights;
d. to protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
e. to provide services and protection to women and children victims of acts of violence and discrimination, reporters, and witnesses; and
f. to facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

